-- `matches!`'s second argument is a **pattern**, and Redox has no way to pass
-- one — so a method asking *is this one of these variants* is a `case` with a
-- `_ -> false` arm. Seven of them here: `TokenKind`'s two predicates,
-- `TriviaKind::is_doc`, and four one-line tests inside the scanners.
--
-- `redox-ast`, `redox-fmt` and `redox-diag` carry the same allow for the same
-- reason — plan 68 found it, and only a row making `matches!` reachable would
-- retire it.
#![allow(clippy::match_like_matches_macro)]

-- The same gap one step over: Redox has no `if let`, so *do this if it
-- matches* is a `case` with a `_ -> ()` arm. Three of them, each where the
-- Rust wrote `if let Some(x) = …`.
#![allow(clippy::single_match)]

-- Plan 55 §1.6 requires a `()`-returning body to **end with `()`** rather than
-- implying it — deliberately, so that a body ending in a loop, a binding or an
-- assignment cannot become `()` by arriving last. clippy reads that `()` as a
-- statement with no effect. The two rules disagree by design, and §1.6's is
-- the one with an argument behind it.
#![allow(clippy::no_effect)]

-- The same `()`, in the places clippy names differently: `return ()` and a
-- `()` closing a `case` arm.
#![allow(clippy::unused_unit)]

-- ! `redox-lexer` — the off-side-rule lexer.
-- !
-- ! Plan 01 (`docs/05 - 01 - Vertical Slice.md`) leaf 2 built the minimum;
-- ! plan 02 (`docs/07 - 02 - Lexical Surface.md`) finished the lexical surface
-- ! of `docs/03 - Redox Surface Design.md` §4 and §11.
-- !
-- ! Hand-written rather than built on `logos`: a regex-dispatch lexer cannot
-- ! express an off-side rule, and continuation suppression is lexer *state*
-- ! carried across lines (`docs/COMPILER.md` §2).
-- !
-- ! Three properties are mandatory and must not be weakened by later plans:
-- !
-- ! 1. **Every token carries a byte [`Span`]** — including tokens inside a
-- !    string interpolation, whose spans index the original file.
-- ! 2. **Comments, doc comments and fences become [`Trivia`] attached to the
-- !    following token, never discarded.**
-- ! 3. **Every token records whether whitespace preceded it**
-- !    ([`Token::ws_before`]), which doc 03 §5.1's call grammar and §5.4's
-- !    `(-1)`-versus-`(- 1)` rule both depend on.
-- !
-- ! This crate decides *what tokens exist*, not what they mean. A token no
-- ! parser yet accepts is expected, not dead.
-- !
-- ! Layout follows `docs/06 - Redox Code Architecture.md`: one construct per
-- ! file, grouped into a module tree, modules private, public items
-- ! re-exported here so callers see a flat namespace.

-- | Tokenize a source.
module lex
-- | The off-side-rule scanner.
module lexer

-- | A token, its span, and the trivia preceding it.
module token
-- | Non-semantic source text that must survive to the emitter.
module trivia
-- | The body of a `"""…"""` literal, undecoded.
module verbatim_triple

export import lex::error::LexError
export import lex::lex
export import redox_diag::Span
export import token::Token
export import token::keyword::Keyword
export import token::kind::TokenKind
export import token::str_part::StrPart
export import trivia::Trivia
export import trivia::kind::TriviaKind
export import verbatim_triple::verbatim_triple
